        "order": "3.09",
        "review_scope": "Pages 1\u20132 applicability and initial filing; appendix paragraph 11 conferral, pages 4\u20135. Other appendix deadlines collected but not substantively abstracted.",
        "stated_effective_date": "2026-01-20",
        "stated_issuance_date": "2026-01-12",
        "summary": "Applies to civil actions except Rule 1.200(a) exclusions. The plaintiff signs and files the standing case-management order with the complaint and serves it on named defendants; the clerk is directed not to accept filing without it. Appendix paragraph 11 requires substantive good-faith conferral before any motion, with date/time certification; an unsuccessful-attempt statement must detail at least three attempts within the immediately preceding one-month period. Original contains track and schedule details."
      },
